BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Community Health & Fun Fair
DTSTART:20260813T160000
DTEND:20260813T190000
DTSTAMP:20260813T120603Z
UID:72212f6507819d20f5d737d064933a@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:This FREE fun\, family-friendly event is open to all ages and 
 will feature a wide range of health and wellness activities\, including:<b
 r/><br/>• Free Backpacks!<br/>• Free health screenings<br/>• Communi
 ty resource tables<br/>• Massages from Shiatsu School of Vermont<br/>•
  Professional Facepainting by Blossom Winks<br/>• Bounce House and Obsta
 cle Course<br/>• Photobooth from VT NH Photobooth<br/>• Bubble Station
  with GIANT bubbles<br/>• Food for purchase from 802 Soul Kitchen<br/>
 • More to come!!<br/><br/>Whether you’re looking for health screenings
 \, family activities\, or just a fun way to spend an evening\, there’s s
 omething for everyone.\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Fairs\, Festivals & Markets
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/community-
 health-fun-fair-08-07-2026-15-57-40
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Notorious
DTSTART:20260813T190000
DTEND:20260813T235900
DTSTAMP:20260813T120603Z
UID:e0b71a8906915d36dd4ef36aa2e7b8@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Happy Birthday\, Alfred Hitchcock<br/><br/>Sir Alfred Hitchcoc
 k turns 127 on August 13 so we’ll sing a few rounds of “Happy Birthday
 ” and watch one of his many\, many masterpieces: Notorious.<br/><br/>Car
 y Grant and Ingrid Bergman show what movie stars can do\, as they burn a h
 ole in the screen with their off-the-chart chemistry. To say the camera lo
 ves them is a woeful understatement. The plot has U.S. government agent De
 vlin (Grant) pressuring the guilt-ridden alcoholic Alicia (Bergman) into s
 leeping with a Nazi (Claude Rains) to learn secrets about plutonium. There
  are set pieces galore—That three-minute kiss! That tracking shot to the
  key! The journey down the staircase!—and the supporting players are a d
 elight\, but the real focus is Bergman and Grant. The witty\, literate scr
 ipt by Ben Hecht (co-scripted by an uncredited Hitch)\, the fine score by 
 Roy Webb (Bernard Herrmann was unavailable)\, and beautiful B&amp\;W photo
 graphy by Ted Tetzlaff are all top-notch\, a real testament to Hollywood f
 ilmmaking at its finest.<br/>\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Film
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/notorious-
 30-07-2026-10-59-07
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Panel Discussion: Into Light Project
DTSTART:20260813T193000
DTEND:20260813T235900
DTSTAMP:20260813T120603Z
UID:525629a6f0c7e9a582ad2445111d47@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Presented in connection with the exhibition Into Light Project
 \, this panel discussion brings together people in recovery to share their
  lived experiences with substance use disorders and the ongoing process of
  healing. Through conversation and audience Q&amp\;A\, panelists will refl
 ect on the challenges they’ve faced\, the support they’ve found\, and 
 the perspectives they’ve gained along the way. Whether you have personal
  experience with substance use\, are supporting a loved one\, or simply wa
 nt to better understand the recovery journey\, this event offers an opport
 unity to listen\, learn\, and connect.<br/><br/>In collaboration with Turn
 ing Point of Windham County\, Brattleboro Police Department\, Project C.A.
 R.E.\, and Community Substance Use Response (CSUR)<br/><br/>ADMISSION: Fre
 e<br/>Registration recommended\; walk-ins welcome\, space permitting<br/>T
 o register\, click here or call 802-257-0124 x101<br/><br/>LOCATION:<br/>I
 n person at BMAC (10 Vernon Street\, Brattleboro VT 05301)<br/><br/>ACCESS
 IBILITY QUESTIONS?<br/>Email office@brattleboromuseum.org or call 802-257-
 0124 x101\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Art & Museum Exhibits
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/panel-disc
 ussion-into-light-project-16-07-2026-11-01-44
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Pure Prairie League
DTSTART:20260813T193000
DTEND:20260813T213000
DTSTAMP:20260813T120603Z
UID:289f87d2546dc3b8adb173941626f7@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:From their beginnings in mid-sixties Ohio as a group of friend
 s playing cover tunes to the present-day unit featuring the propulsive tea
 m of drummer Scott Thompson and bassist Jared Camic\, keyboard master Rand
 y Harper\, guitar ace/vocalist Jeff Zona and pedal steel/saxophonist John 
 Heinrich\, Pure Prairie League continues to embellish the rich 50-plus yea
 r history of one of Country-Rock’s pioneering forces. As one reviewer re
 cently wrote: “PPL’s sound combines sweet memories with edgy\, contemp
 orary muscle. Their vocals are as strong as Kentucky moonshine and the mus
 icianship and performance skills are as sharp as a straight razor”.\n\nS
 ources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Music: Rock\, Folk\, Jazz and More
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/pure-prair
 ie-league-21-05-2026-15-13-44
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Maple Tree Place FREE Concert on the Green Presenting The John
  Fogerty Tribute Project!
DTSTART:20260813T180000
DTEND:20260813T200000
DTSTAMP:20260813T120603Z
UID:bc7a56ff020cfbe5e1e9bf9ca2238d@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:You may be asking “Who'll Stop the Rain”\, the answer is T
 he John Fogerty Tribute Project who is our third Free concert and amazing 
 tribute band of the Summer Concert Series here at Maple Tree Place\, it’
 s just “Up Around the Bend”!!!<br/><br/>You are going to want to be 
 “Centerfield” on Thursday\, 8-13-26\, starting at 6:00 PM here at Mapl
 e Tree Place\, On The Green. Join us as we are "Rockin' All Over the World
 " from the comfort of our backyard. We fell Like a “Fortunate Son” bei
 ng able to hear this “ Travelin' Band”\, we feel like “Proud Mary”
  being able to bring this group into town. <br/><br/>Next week's band is t
 he one and only The John Fogerty Tribute Project: A CCR and John Fogerty T
 ribute!<br/> <br/>The John Fogerty Tribute Project is not a cookie cutter 
 tribute act giving you the same songs and robot style performances. Rather
 \, their live\, interactive\, heart throbbing performances are at the core
  of a real live John Fogerty concert. An energetic tribute that will bring
  the house down with all the songs you would expect to hear from both John
  Fogerty’s Creedence Clearwater Revival years and his solo career\, in t
 his unforgettable tribute performance On The Green at Maple Tree Place. <b
 r/> <br/>Bring your chairs\, blankets\, and come early to check out all th
 e changes here at MTP. New stores include J. Crew Factory\, Bob’s Discou
 nt Furniture\, Boot Barn\, and Four Sisters. This is a great time for the 
 entire family\; choose from a variety of tasty dining options with outdoor
  seating at Grazers and McGillicuddy’s\, or cool down with some FroYo\, 
 from Yogurt City. You can also order your meal to go On The Green while yo
 u enjoy the show!<br/><br/>As always\, Vermont weather may be a factor dow
 n the road\, so we will do our best to keep everyone in the loop if any de
 lays or reschedules are needed.<br/>\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Music: Rock\, Folk\, Jazz and More
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/the-maple-
 tree-place-free-concert-on-the-green-presenting-the-john-fogerty-tribute-p
 roject-29-07-2026-22-28-57
END:VEVENT
